From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: run a tapped notification action only if the unlock directly follows
Description:
 A notification action tapped on the lock screen, or in the action drawer
 over it, waits for the unlock. It was dropped only after a failed or
 successful attempt, so closing the keypad again or the display turning
 off kept it: a much later unlock, independent of the tap, ran it.
 .
 The lock screen now reports leaving the keypad without unlocking (keypad
 back at its closed position, display off) as unlockCancelled() and
 drops its own pending action then. It also tells the shell through the
 new D-Bus method cancelLockScreenUnlock() of org.kde.plasmashell (signal
 lockScreenUnlockCancelled), which drops the action held by the action
 drawer. A wrong PIN keeps the action while the keypad stays open. An
 unlock with the fingerprint is the same as with the PIN.
 .
 Without authentication (the session can be unlocked at once) the lock
 screen quit when the keypad was opened without running the pending
 action; it goes through the same path as an authenticated unlock now.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL-2.0-or-later, GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
